Miracles do still happen.

This week was my last one in Tsuyama. A lot of stuff happened...

Monday-Tuesday
We had district Pday and In-Person District Council Meeting! For Pday we
went to the Sand Museum (second time for me and one other district member)
as well as get some sushi for lunch. In person DCM was great too! On the
way back to Tsuyama we talked to a couple High Schoolers at the station,
and made them some art for them. It was a fun interaction for sure!

Wednesday-Thursday
Getting to do one last Kids Eikaiwa class was a blast! For some reason
everyone was actually kind of into it this time, and 2 new kids were there
too! Sister Morimoto had us do a cute activity where we cut paper to make a
star, with only one straight cut! (She prepared the paper beforehand and
folded it so that happened)

Friday-Sunday!
Listen to the recording!!

I got transferred to a place called Gobo, it's mad Country! My new
companion is Elder Warnick, looking forward to getting to know him =F0=9F=
=94=A5

Have a great Christmas everyone =E2=9D=A4=EF=B8=8F=E2=9D=A4=EF=B8=8F

I love you!

--000000000000dc14fa06469dd11f
